   128	+/* ---- delete tests (M2) --------------------------------------------------
   129	+ * rb_delete has to handle several tree shapes, and a test cannot see node
   130	+ * colors. So each case picks an insertion order whose resulting shape is
   131	+ * forced by the insert rules -- every shape below was dumped from a debug
   132	+ * build, not guessed -- then deletes the key sitting in the target spot.
   133	+ *
   134	+ * What a test CAN see from outside: the return code, rb_size, rb_find on
   135	+ * every key (values are distinct malloc'd ints, so found vs. absent is
   136	+ * unambiguous), counting_free (a delete frees exactly one value),
   137	+ * rb_validate (a black leaf that is simply unlinked breaks rule 5 -> code 7,
   138	+ * so validate is what proves the fixup ran), and rb_debug_live_allocs (the
   139	+ * node and its key copy both came back).
